   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Dear group members, good morning</div><div>    I am having another &quot;novice&quot; question. I am trying to plot the results of the minimized truth table with pimplot and QCA radar function. Yet I have the same mistake every time.</div><div>\r\n\r\n<span role=\"presentation\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;padding-left:6px;padding-bottom:8px;line-height:1.2;border:medium none;outline:none;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;width:1251.26px\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"><span><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;line-height:1.2;font-size:10pt;vertical-align:top\" align=\"left\"><br><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:10pt;outline:none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:blue\">pimplot(data = INNOV2added,outcome = &quot;highpatent&quot;,results = solT,all_labels = TRUE,jitter = TRUE,fontsize = 6)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in `[.data.frame`(results$tt$recoded.data, , outcome) : \r\n  undefined columns selected\r\n</span></span></span></span></span><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;line-height:1.2;font-size:10pt;vertical-align:top\" align=\"left\"></span></span></span></span>\r\n\r\n<span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:blue\">QCAradar(results = solT,outcome = &quot;highpatent&quot;,fit = FALSE)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in `[.data.frame`(results$tt$recoded.data, , outcome) : \r\n  undefined columns selected</span></span></span> <br></div><div><br><span role=\"presentation\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;padding-left:6px;padding-bottom:8px;line-height:1.2;border:medium none;outline:none;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;width:1251.26px\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"><span>If I understand correctly, it is something wrong with the way outcome is presented (i.e. &quot;highpatent&quot; is not &quot;dropping down&quot; after I type &quot;outcome=&quot;.</span></span></div><div><span role=\"presentation\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;padding-left:6px;padding-bottom:8px;line-height:1.2;border:medium none;outline:none;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;width:1251.26px\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"><span>When I was minimizing the truth table there were not problems with &quot;highpatent&quot; as outcome.</span></span></div><div><span role=\"presentation\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;padding-left:6px;padding-bottom:8px;line-height:1.2;border:medium none;outline:none;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;width:1251.26px\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\"><span>Your advice is very much appreciated!<br></span></span></div>"
    ]
