   "subject": "Re: [QCA] pimplotfunction",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n  \r\n    \r\n    \r\n  \r\n  <div style=\"padding-bottom:1px\">\r\n    <p><font face=\"Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\">Dear Alexander,</font></p>\r\n    <p>pimplot() and truthTable() belong to different packages, so\r\n      getting an error message for one function and not the other can\r\n      happen. <br>\r\n    </p>\r\n    <p>The message reads such that there is no column highpatent in the\r\n      results object that could be fed into the plotting function. I\r\n      remember I once had the same problem, but, unfortunately, I don&#39;t\r\n      remember whether and how I could fix it. You may check the column\r\n      names in solT$tt$recoded.data to see whether highpatent is\r\n      included. It could be an upper-case/lower-case issue, but I don&#39;t\r\n      think so because this should happen to everyone.</p>\r\n    <p>I am sorry I don&#39;t have a quick fix to offer.<br>\r\n    </p>\r\n    <p>Kind regards</p>\r\n    <p>Ingo<br>\r\n    </p></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"padding-bottom:1px\">\r\n    <p><br>\r\n    </p>\r\n    <div>Am 22.03.2023 um 10:26 schrieb\r\n      Alexander Strelkov:<br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    </div>"
    ],
